    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Raised in Muhammad's household, Ali was among the first to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, married Muhammad's daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatima">Fatima</a> and served as his secretary, deputy and standard-bearer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>.</li><li>After Muhammad's death in 632 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> and Shia Muslims tell the succession differently: Sunnis accept Abu Bakr's appointment, while Shia Muslims hold that Muhammad had designated Ali at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghadir-khumm">Ghadir Khumm</a>.</li><li>Ali became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in 656 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uthman-ibn-affan">Uthman</a>'s assassination, fought civil wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aisha">Aisha</a>, Talha, Zubayr and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Mu'awiya</a>, and was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a> in 661, after which Mu'awiya founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Ali's own father, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-talib-ibn-abd-al-muttalib">Abu Talib</a>, raised Muhammad, and Ali later came under Muhammad's guardianship when he was about five years old.</p></aside>
    </section>

